  "UNVERIFIED: written from documented output, not run against a device. Every value below is copied from Cisco's NX-API CLI reference; `| json` over the CLI returns the same `body` the pages show, which the cliconf plugin decodes before the playbook sees it.",
  "show interface status | json: https://developer.cisco.com/docs/nx-api-cli-reference-for-the-cisco-nexus-7000-series-platform/interface-commands (rows mgmt0, Ethernet9/1..9/4 of the 'show interface status' example). The page's example has no `name` key (a configured description); the parser reads it when present.",
  "show interface switchport | json: same page, 'show int switchport' example (rows Ethernet9/1, Ethernet9/2, port-channel12), counters omitted: none are shown. That example has only access ports; the trunk branch is covered in test_ports_parse.py with a copy that changes oper_mode.",
  "show ip interface vrf all | json: https://developer.cisco.com/docs/nx-api-cli-reference-for-the-cisco-nexus-3500-series-platform/ip-interface-commands/ ('show ip interface 89.1.4.1' example, packet counters left out). The page shows the single-VRF shape; the parser finds rows at any depth, which test_ports_parse.py checks with the rows wrapped in a per-VRF table.",
  "show lldp neighbors detail | json: https://developer.cisco.com/docs/nx-api-cli-reference-for-the-cisco-nexus-3500-series-platform/lldp-commands ('show lldp neighbors detail' example, rows mgmt0, Eth1/2, Eth1/4; LLDP prints the short port names).",
  "show inventory | json: https://developer.cisco.com/docs/nx-api-cli-reference-for-the-cisco-nexus-9000-series-platform/inventory-commands (the whole example; the page shows names and descriptions wrapped in quotes and the parser strips them). No transceiver row is in it."
